When generating a Git commit message for this repository, output only
the message below. commitlint rejects the commit otherwise.

<type>[optional scope]: <description>

<body>

Rules:
- English. Conventional Commits.
- Types: build, chore, ci, docs, feat, fix, perf, refactor, revert,
  style, test.
- Scope is optional and lowercase, such as ci(circleci) or feat(home).
- Description: imperative mood, lowercase, no trailing period.
- The whole header is at most 72 characters.
- Blank line between the header and the body.
- Body: what changed and why. Hard-wrap every line at 72 characters.
  Count them. A body or footer line over 100 characters fails commitlint.
  Never leave the body as one long line.
- No markdown, no file list, and no bullet list of the diff.
- Do not add ! or a BREAKING CHANGE footer. The project stays on 0.x
  until the e-commerce launch.

Example:

fix(contact): keep the WhatsApp number out of client components

The number now comes only from the server route, so it never ships
in the page bundle.
